WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.160
Libraries, I think, can have an amazing role to play

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.020
because they are like tanks full of knowledge

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.200
so knowledge banks, if, you want,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.760
and the thing is, though, that libraries very often

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.400
tend to be, sort of, retroactive in terms of looking back.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.660
Maybe one could think of a library as about

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.680
producing the future.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.060
Maybe an archive of old stuff.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.480
It's not really about going back in time.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.860
Maybe the archive is also 
about using it about

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.060
going into the future.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.380
And then that way, a library could 
really be a time machine

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.260
through which we can look into, 
well, what do we need to do

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.660
about changing things in the future.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.300
And I guess that also means reconsidering

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.100
the, you know, the fact that libraries are very often

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.400
very stiff and inflexible, and, 
you know, they need to re -

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.480
They need to reconsider how to 
reach out to people

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.860
But clearly, libraries are amazing
resourceful systems,

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.060
which we just need to activate.

